@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature: OSB Product
	Testing OSB Product functionality on sandbox.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay DXP Product    |
	| A Liferay Portal Product |
	* I tear down the following products on the sandbox
	| A Liferay DXP Product    |
	| A Liferay Portal Product |

Scenario: Update and delete product
	Products updated on OSB that are no longer linked to a Koroneiki product key should also be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I update a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"

Scenario: Update and delete product with external link
	Products updated on OSB that are no longer linked to a Koroneiki product key should also be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I update a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"

Scenario: Update and delete product updated via Koroneiki
	Products updated via Koroneiki that are also updated on OSB that are no longer linked to a Koroneiki product key should also be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I update a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product"
	And I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"

Scenario: Attempt to delete linked product
	Products linked to Koroneiki should not be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |

Scenario: Attempt to delete linked product with external link
	Products with external links linked to Koroneiki should not be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name                      | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key     | Verify from name      |
	| External Link Domain      | liferaydxp            |
	| External Link Entity Id   | 1234                  |
	| External Link Entity Name | LiferayDXP            |

Scenario: Attempt to delete linked product updated via Koroneiki
	Products updated via Koroneiki that are linked to Koroneiki should not be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |
	And I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"

Scenario: Add back deleted product
	Products removed from OSB should be able to be added back via OSB

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I update a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I add a product on the sandbox with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |

Scenario: Add back deleted updated product
	Updated products removed from OSB should be able to be added back via OSB

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I update a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product"
	And I add a product on the sandbox with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |

Scenario: Attempt to delete added back product
	Products removed and added back via OSB should not be removable via OSB

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I update a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I add a product on the sandbox with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product |
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |

Scenario: Attempt to delete updated and added back product
	Updated products removed and added back via OSB should not be removable via OSB

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I update a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product"
	And I add a product on the sandbox with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product |
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |